# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Voice Agents test bench — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your keys.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored; never commit real keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Bland.ai ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From https://app.bland.ai/ → Settings / API keys.
# Bland handles telephony itself, so this key alone is enough to
# place a real outbound test call.
BLAND_API_KEY=

# ── ElevenLabs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From https://elevenlabs.io/ → Profile → API key.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs places outbound calls through a Twilio number that you
# link inside the ElevenLabs "Conversational AI / Agents" dashboard.
#
# 1. Create an agent in ElevenLabs and copy its Agent ID here.
#    (This app overrides the agent's prompt + first message per call,
#     so a single reusable "test" agent is fine. Make sure the agent's
#     Security settings allow overrides for "System prompt" and
#     "First message".)
ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# 2. Link a Twilio phone number to that agent and copy the
#    "Phone number ID" that ElevenLabs assigns it here.
ELEVENLABS_AGENT_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# ── Vapi ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From https://dashboard.vapi.ai/ → API Keys (use a private key).
# Vapi compiles the whole call script into an inline assistant, so it's
# nearly as plug-and-play as Bland — you just need one phone number.
VAPI_API_KEY=

# In Vapi → Phone Numbers, grab a free Vapi number (or import one) and
# copy its ID here. Calls are placed from this number.
VAPI_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# Optional: the LLM the Vapi assistant runs on. Defaults below.
# Make sure the matching provider key is configured in your Vapi dashboard.
# VAPI_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai
# VAPI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# ── OpenAI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The "OpenAI" provider runs OpenAI's Realtime speech-to-speech model
# (gpt-realtime — their best voice) on a real phone call. OpenAI has no
# telephony of its own, so the call is placed over Vapi's transport:
# it reuses VAPI_API_KEY + VAPI_PHONE_NUMBER_ID above.
#
# IMPORTANT: add your OpenAI API key in the Vapi dashboard under
# Provider Keys, so Vapi can reach the Realtime model on your behalf.
#
# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-realtime
# OPENAI_VOICE=marin        # try cedar or alloy if a voice id is rejected
